   206	def rebuild_jsonl(source: Path, target: Path) -> RebuildResult:
   207	    """Rebuild a fresh sqlite store at ``target`` from the JSONL log ``source``.
   208	
   209	    Rebuilding an index from its log is ``engine.jsonl_store``'s own job —
   210	    it is what :class:`~engine.jsonl_store.JsonlStore` does on every open
   211	    whose offset marker cannot be trusted, and it is where the recovery
   212	    rules (verbatim insert, no re-mint, the engine's own INSERT SQL) already
   213	    live. This is the migration-side wrapper around that, and it adds the
   214	    two guarantees the live path cannot make about a *migration* source:
   215	
   216	    - the source is **read-only evidence**. It is fully parsed first
   217	      (:func:`_validate_log`), and a torn tail is raised, not truncated —
   218	      see there for why the live log's repair semantics do not carry over.
   219	      Because validation has proven the log clean, the construction below
   220	      cannot reach the truncation path or fail mid-codec;
   221	    - a failed rebuild leaves **no target**. Partial sqlite bytes would make
